1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
You

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,200
Hey, what's up?

3
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:15,400
You want to practice with me?

4
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:26,500
Don't look at me like that. Do do I want to do what with you practice?

5
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:32,900
For blocking practice. It's free practice time. You want to do something besides shagging balls, right?

6
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:39,000
Look if you don't want to it's fine. Sookie's coming too!

7
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:43,760
Glad you could join us!

8
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:51,720
Sweet! Put those down first. Oh

9
00:00:57,500 --> 00:00:59,500
Oh

10
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:03,600
Hey

11
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:08,620
Oh

12
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:13,280
Hey

13
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:43,260
We'll be right back.

14
00:01:43,280 --> 00:02:13,260
We'll be right back.

15
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:43,260
We'll be right back.

16
00:02:43,260 --> 00:03:13,240
We'll be right back.

17
00:03:13,740 --> 00:03:16,180
I haven't seen the video yet.

18
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:19,080
How did Shiratorizawa lose to you?

19
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:22,340
Was Ushuaka off his game or something?

20
00:03:22,340 --> 00:03:28,120
He seemed to play just fine to me.

21
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:29,120
Yeah?

22
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:31,680
Then how do you explain the loss?

23
00:03:31,820 --> 00:03:33,420
What kind of tricks did you play?

24
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:35,240
Or did someone actually stop him?

25
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:42,000
Honestly, yeah, someone did stop him.

26
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:44,460
If you can call what Hinata did a stop.

27
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:47,600
Who did?

28
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:49,000
What year is he in?

29
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:49,960
What's his name?

30
00:03:50,180 --> 00:03:51,460
Where did he go to middle school?

31
00:03:51,460 --> 00:03:52,220
Sorry about him.

32
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:54,980
He's just an incredibly serious pessimist, guys.

33
00:03:55,180 --> 00:03:59,220
If someone is ever a threat to him, he gets freaked out and he loses his mind.

34
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:01,540
I'm not a pessimist at all.

35
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:02,960
I'm simply cautious.

36
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:06,980
Is that why you haven't actually given 100% here yet?

37
00:04:06,980 --> 00:04:11,840
What makes you say that?

38
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:13,500
It's just a hunch.

39
00:04:14,700 --> 00:04:17,380
I'd say you've been about average here so far.

40
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:24,100
He's convinced that there's been something terribly wrong with his shoulders lately.

41
00:04:24,100 --> 00:04:28,600
But, well, of course, in his case, it's usually all in his head.

42
00:04:28,940 --> 00:04:31,820
That said, there's nothing wrong with being cautious, is there?

43
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:32,560
Bath time.

44
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:32,960
Huh?

45
00:04:33,620 --> 00:04:34,100
Already?

46
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:38,900
I'm getting in and out before anyone else can fill the tub with their charms.

47
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:41,900
Sorry to bug you guys.

48
00:04:43,840 --> 00:04:44,860
Oh, man.

49
00:04:45,180 --> 00:04:47,880
He's one of the top three in Japan, and you call him average?

50
00:04:49,820 --> 00:04:52,640
I said that he's been average so far.

51
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:59,540
Everyone here is really good.

52
00:05:00,440 --> 00:05:02,500
And that guy there has been great.

53
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:04,180
I wonder who he is.

54
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:16,180
But, you know, this first year training camp has been something else.

55
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:21,020
To be honest, I'm not really sure why Coach is having it.

56
00:05:21,740 --> 00:05:22,100
Hmm.

57
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:23,340
I don't know.

58
00:05:23,340 --> 00:05:26,300
I think Coach Washijo is just trying to change.

59
00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:30,160
Otherwise, he would have never given a second thought to holding an elite camp.

60
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:34,560
And if he had held one, he certainly wouldn't have considered making you the head coach of it.

61
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:35,240
Think about it.

62
00:05:35,980 --> 00:05:40,520
That said, something has been different about him ever since the game against Karasuno.

63
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:44,060
You think maybe their number 10 got into his head?

64
00:05:44,060 --> 00:05:47,880
Well, the kid's definitely on his radar now.

65
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:50,560
Because, come on, man.

66
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:54,900
Did you see the look Coach Washijo had when number 10 got that last point?

67
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:58,100
That look I won't be forgetting anytime soon.

68
00:05:58,100 --> 00:06:18,380
I mean, I expected to see him mortified.

69
00:06:18,380 --> 00:06:21,760
But instead, I saw something else.

70
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:23,860
Thanks for waiting.

71
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:25,280
Here are your raw oysters.

72
00:06:26,020 --> 00:06:27,060
There they are.

73
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:28,000
Mmm.

74
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:30,420
Hey, you better be careful with those.

75
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:33,680
You remember that time when our high school coach wound up with food poisoning?

76
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:37,020
And we all got to enjoy freak practice for the next day on.

77
00:06:37,520 --> 00:06:38,800
Ah, such sweet memories.

78
00:06:39,260 --> 00:06:39,620
Mmm.

79
00:06:39,960 --> 00:06:40,320
Oh.

80
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:42,860
Left side!

81
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:44,240
Got it!

82
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:56,880
Hang on a second.

83
00:06:57,060 --> 00:06:58,340
Hinata, you're not a libero?

84
00:06:58,820 --> 00:06:59,300
Huh?

85
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:01,200
You think I could be a libero?

86
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:02,740
You think I'm good at receiving?

87
00:07:02,740 --> 00:07:04,180
Oh, no.

88
00:07:04,420 --> 00:07:05,780
I didn't really mean it like that.

89
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:07,540
Wait, then what did you mean?

90
00:07:07,860 --> 00:07:09,080
I want to block two.

91
00:07:09,460 --> 00:07:10,500
Two middle blockers?

92
00:07:10,900 --> 00:07:14,420
If the ball comes to me, I'll slam it down on their faces.

93
00:07:15,180 --> 00:07:15,460
Ah!

94
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:18,200
Ooh, me too.

95
00:07:18,820 --> 00:07:19,260
Seriously?

96
00:07:20,180 --> 00:07:20,740
Ahem.

97
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:29,640
Bring it on.

98
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:30,520
I'll block anything.

99
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:31,840
Same over here.

100
00:07:32,740 --> 00:07:33,180
Ahem.

101
00:07:43,180 --> 00:07:43,660
Damn.

102
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:45,480
Am I the shortest one here?

103
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:51,300
That was so cool!

104
00:07:51,300 --> 00:07:57,940
Our side placement was wrong for that play.

105
00:07:58,320 --> 00:07:59,480
The line shot was open.

106
00:07:59,700 --> 00:07:59,940
Ah!

107
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:03,100
Well, I was sure he was going to do a cross shot, okay?

108
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:04,420
Yeah, me too.

109
00:08:05,700 --> 00:08:06,400
Same here.

110
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:08,980
I thought it looked like a cross shot as well.

111
00:08:10,340 --> 00:08:13,940
He even ran in a zigzag, like he was getting ready to do a cut.

112
00:08:13,940 --> 00:08:15,280
He really is good.

113
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:16,420
He really is good.

114
00:08:17,860 --> 00:08:20,740
I heard he hasn't been playing volleyball long either.

115
00:08:21,380 --> 00:08:22,880
The date tech training shows.

116
00:08:23,220 --> 00:08:25,080
He's not jumping around at random.

117
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:25,820
Hey, Tsukishima.

118
00:08:25,820 --> 00:08:28,000
Hey, Tsukishima.

119
00:08:29,540 --> 00:08:35,360
So, before, when you invited me to play, did you do it so I'd get a chance to spike?

120
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:35,800
No.

121
00:08:35,800 --> 00:08:35,860
No.

122
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:37,000
Okay.

123
00:08:38,760 --> 00:08:46,120
At the Nationals, when we're playing against those high-level teams, the battles between blockers and spikers are going to be even more intense.

124
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:46,340
Okay.

125
00:08:46,340 --> 00:08:52,060
But tactics aside, it's clear that Hinata is a spiker who knows how to read a block.

126
00:08:52,980 --> 00:08:55,500
I'd be an idiot not to practice against him.

127
00:09:01,360 --> 00:09:02,000
Got it!

128
00:09:06,140 --> 00:09:07,020
Nice kill!

129
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:11,480
If the ball is going to go over the net, you don't have to worry about making a perfect pass.

130
00:09:11,580 --> 00:09:12,000
Yes, sir!

131
00:09:12,620 --> 00:09:14,220
And that was a nice set, Kageyama.

132
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:16,560
But you can stand a little farther from the net.

133
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:16,980
What?

134
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:18,000
Yes, sir!

135
00:09:24,420 --> 00:09:25,680
That was a nice kill.

136
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:28,280
Kageyama there.

137
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:31,760
He had no trouble whatsoever adjusting to a lefty-middle blocker.

138
00:09:32,180 --> 00:09:34,240
His technique and game sets are both phenomenal.

139
00:09:34,980 --> 00:09:35,980
How is that set?

140
00:09:36,580 --> 00:09:36,940
Hmm.

141
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:39,680
I think I could probably hit it a little bit faster.

142
00:09:39,940 --> 00:09:41,140
So a little zippier, maybe?

143
00:09:41,340 --> 00:09:42,240
And, like, more compact?

144
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:43,400
I can do that.

145
00:09:44,220 --> 00:09:48,520
He just says, I can do that, and then he actually does it?

146
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:50,060
That's kind of spooky.

147
00:09:51,140 --> 00:09:52,860
So, um, keep passing.

148
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:53,940
Just like that, okay?

149
00:09:54,340 --> 00:09:55,040
You got it.

150
00:09:55,520 --> 00:09:58,900
I'm pretty sure communication is not Kageyama's strong suit.

151
00:09:59,260 --> 00:10:01,360
But you can tell that he's actually trying.

152
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:06,560
Front! Front!

153
00:10:07,760 --> 00:10:08,200
Nice!

154
00:10:08,200 --> 00:10:17,680
Left!

155
00:10:17,680 --> 00:10:21,680
That was high!

156
00:10:21,680 --> 00:10:33,720
Oh, that was high.

157
00:10:36,780 --> 00:10:38,000
That was in.

158
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:38,860
Fantastic.

159
00:10:38,860 --> 00:10:51,880
Make sure you stretch properly, guys.

160
00:10:56,680 --> 00:10:57,120
Hey.

161
00:10:58,680 --> 00:11:03,680
So, like, do you recognize me or know who the hell I am?

162
00:11:04,940 --> 00:11:06,780
Yeah, we met the first day I got here.

163
00:11:06,820 --> 00:11:07,920
That's not what I meant, bro.

164
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:11,760
What I'm asking you is whether or not you've seen any of my games before.

165
00:11:11,900 --> 00:11:12,860
Don't think so.

166
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:16,160
There's another guy trying to pick a fight with Kageyama.

167
00:11:16,620 --> 00:11:18,320
Freak out a little bit, all right?

168
00:11:18,440 --> 00:11:19,240
Be shocked!

169
00:11:19,460 --> 00:11:20,720
You've been all staring at me like,

170
00:11:20,860 --> 00:11:23,440
since the second I walked in the damn door!

171
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:29,000
Most people just assume that I can't hack it because of how small I am.

172
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:31,980
Then they see me play and totally freak out!

173
00:11:32,440 --> 00:11:34,820
That is the normal course of events, okay?

174
00:11:34,820 --> 00:11:39,300
This guy's gonna be real fun to put up with.

175
00:11:40,860 --> 00:11:42,320
I am freaking out.

176
00:11:42,500 --> 00:11:42,760
Hmm?

177
00:11:43,060 --> 00:11:45,960
But also, learning from you, too.

178
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:46,860
Ha!

179
00:11:46,860 --> 00:11:51,900
Well, well, well, well.

180
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:53,520
You have nerves of steel.

181
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:55,800
Setter.

182
00:11:56,340 --> 00:11:57,120
Second year.

183
00:11:58,080 --> 00:11:59,020
Latsumu Miya.

184
00:11:59,480 --> 00:12:01,640
You know, Kageyama, my first read on you

185
00:12:01,640 --> 00:12:05,120
is that you're as prickly as a cactus right down to the soles of your feet.

186
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:11,140
But on the court, well, you're just a goody-two-shoes.

187
00:12:12,740 --> 00:12:13,220
Huh?

188
00:12:13,220 --> 00:12:39,000
Here's your drink.

189
00:12:39,320 --> 00:12:39,960
Thanks, man.

190
00:12:43,580 --> 00:12:44,300
Where's my...

191
00:12:44,300 --> 00:12:45,360
Hey, here's your towel, dude!

192
00:12:45,860 --> 00:12:46,320
All right.

193
00:12:46,700 --> 00:12:48,180
I totally forgot I left it there.

194
00:12:48,540 --> 00:12:49,200
Thanks a lot.

195
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:51,420
Nothing gets past you, Hinata.

196
00:12:57,060 --> 00:12:58,460
Oh, that's gone.

197
00:12:58,860 --> 00:12:59,660
I'll go up and...

198
00:12:59,660 --> 00:13:00,300
I'll go get it!

199
00:13:00,960 --> 00:13:01,280
Okay.

200
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:01,720
Okay.

201
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:01,880
Okay.

202
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:17,080
Watching them play from up here is my new obsession.

203
00:13:25,660 --> 00:13:28,060
Kunimi's receives look a lot like Ushiwaka's.

204
00:13:28,980 --> 00:13:31,080
Every move he makes means something.

205
00:13:34,360 --> 00:13:34,980
Shakuzawa!

206
00:13:36,240 --> 00:13:37,200
Little help?

207
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,920
Or...

208
00:13:41,920 --> 00:13:44,180
Maybe it's just that he doesn't like moving.

209
00:13:44,860 --> 00:13:46,580
He totally just watched it fall.

210
00:13:47,440 --> 00:13:48,080
Come on!

211
00:13:48,180 --> 00:13:49,220
Show us your care, man!

212
00:13:49,660 --> 00:13:51,240
You were supposed to go after that one.

213
00:13:51,560 --> 00:13:53,860
We have the chance to play with a different group of guys here.

214
00:13:54,360 --> 00:13:55,140
Get with it, man!

215
00:13:55,280 --> 00:13:56,480
Go big or go home!

216
00:13:56,480 --> 00:14:04,900
Uh, sorry.

217
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:07,700
I promise, guys, he does try hard when it counts.

218
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:08,500
Now, come on!

219
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:09,060
What's up?

220
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:10,540
You should have gone for that one!

221
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:12,360
Yeah, yeah.

222
00:14:16,700 --> 00:14:17,360
All right.

223
00:14:17,580 --> 00:14:20,360
Go get rehydrated and we'll do some two-on-two drills.

224
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:22,080
Oh, man.

225
00:14:22,520 --> 00:14:24,160
I just can't handle that guy.

226
00:14:24,700 --> 00:14:25,620
You mean Kunimi?

227
00:14:25,940 --> 00:14:28,020
We're all working our butts off at this camp.

228
00:14:28,320 --> 00:14:30,340
And he acts like he doesn't care about any of it.

229
00:14:31,660 --> 00:14:33,380
But, you know...

230
00:14:33,380 --> 00:14:36,500
He's super hard to beat when he starts going all out

231
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:39,120
after saving his energy during the first half of the game.

232
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:42,820
Still, if he can keep the ball in play, he should try.

233
00:14:42,820 --> 00:14:43,540
I know!

234
00:14:43,800 --> 00:14:45,240
He's taking it way too easy!

235
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:46,400
Uh...

236
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:48,720
Easy.

237
00:14:49,540 --> 00:14:49,880
Huh.

238
00:14:50,420 --> 00:14:50,780
Hmm?

239
00:14:53,260 --> 00:14:54,480
Two-on-two, huh?

240
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:56,460
I'm not gonna lie.

241
00:14:56,540 --> 00:14:58,080
Those are the toughest drills we do.

242
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:00,420
Yeah, when there's only two players out there,

243
00:15:00,460 --> 00:15:02,660
you can basically never stop moving around, so...

244
00:15:04,600 --> 00:15:08,620
But the guy who's got it the hardest of everyone

245
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:10,540
is the one sitting over there.

246
00:15:10,540 --> 00:15:12,400
He has almost no experience.

247
00:15:12,820 --> 00:15:15,700
I feel bad saying it,

248
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:18,320
but I don't really want to play with a two-meter guy.

249
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:19,440
Yeah, me neither.

250
00:15:19,660 --> 00:15:21,940
He's tall, but he has the technique of a middle schooler.

251
00:15:22,560 --> 00:15:24,280
Cleaning up after him is a real nightmare.

252
00:15:26,380 --> 00:15:27,340
Gather round!

253
00:15:28,420 --> 00:15:30,080
The rules are exactly the same.

254
00:15:30,340 --> 00:15:31,420
Remember, when you're spiking,

255
00:15:31,580 --> 00:15:33,500
no dinking the ball with the pads of your fingers.

256
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:35,600
First to ten points wins.

257
00:15:35,960 --> 00:15:37,460
And I know I've said this before,

258
00:15:37,460 --> 00:15:40,060
but always make sure you think about your next move.

259
00:15:40,520 --> 00:15:42,500
You won't win if you play without intention.

260
00:15:42,500 --> 00:15:43,260
Yes, sir!

261
00:15:49,920 --> 00:15:50,580
Got it!

262
00:15:53,260 --> 00:15:54,340
Ah, damn it!

263
00:15:54,340 --> 00:16:03,840
That's how you're gonna play?

264
00:16:06,100 --> 00:16:08,860
Kunimi's team is always really good on the two-on-two drills.

265
00:16:09,600 --> 00:16:11,340
He's got good skills, for one thing.

266
00:16:11,680 --> 00:16:14,100
And I can tell he's paying attention to his partner.

267
00:16:14,100 --> 00:16:16,260
But there's something else, too.

268
00:16:16,980 --> 00:16:17,860
I don't know why.

269
00:16:21,860 --> 00:16:24,280
But I feel like he just doesn't get stressed.

270
00:16:24,820 --> 00:16:25,740
Got it over here!

271
00:16:25,740 --> 00:16:32,280
I feel like I'm getting left further and further behind.

272
00:16:32,280 --> 00:16:45,460
I feel like I'm getting left further and further behind.

273
